      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The levels of structural organization in the human body progress from chemical, cellular, tissue, organ, system, to organismal levels.",
        "The cell serves as the fundamental structural and functional unit of life.",
        "Four basic tissue types—epithelial, connective, muscular, and nervous—compose all organs in the human body.",
        "The skeletal system consists of 206 bones partitioned into axial and appendicular divisions."
